{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/531484-twin-scions-of-apollo","id":531484,"title":"Twin Scions of Apollo","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-28T18:37:06-07:00","id":531484,"title":"Twin Scions of Apollo","content":"So I got this player, and this player's got this idea, and her idea is that of a pair of twins, Tina and Tanya. Tina and Tanya are scions of the Sun God.<br /> <br /> The reason I'm here is because we've been tinkering with the idea of having the two characters share the same sheet, acting as a single character with two bodies. they would share the same health, willpower, legend the whole shebang and would lose dots out of each others presence (in their skills to be specific, each one excels at this or that and other skills are simply 'halved'. <br /> <br /> Their single relic will in fact be two, a pendant, one half marked by a small figure of Apollo, the other, of his twin, Artemis. one will grant access to health, sun and prophesy, the other to Moon, Mystery and Darkness. when they're together the pendants share said purviews. <br /> <br /> Is this a bad idea? Should they be separate characters?<br /> <br /> I thought the sharing of everything was reminiscent of the Dioscuri and more than apropos.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T07:49:19-07:00","id":531955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/531484-twin-scions-of-apollo#post531484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I got this player, and this player's got this idea, and her idea is that of a pair of twins, Tina and Tanya. Tina and Tanya are scions of the Sun God.<br /> <br /> The reason I'm here is because we've been tinkering with the idea of having the two characters share the same sheet, acting as a single character with two bodies. they would share the same health, willpower, legend the whole shebang and would lose dots out of each others presence (in their skills to be specific, each one excels at this or that and other skills are simply 'halved'.<br /> <br /> Their single relic will in fact be two, a pendant, one half marked by a small figure of Apollo, the other, of his twin, Artemis. one will grant access to health, sun and prophesy, the other to Moon, Mystery and Darkness. when they're together the pendants share said purviews.<br /> <br /> Is this a bad idea? Should they be separate characters?<br /> <br /> I thought the sharing of everything was reminiscent of the Dioscuri and more than apropos.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems fine to me.<br /> <br /> It could get complicated, but weirdly, there's something similar in 2e that'll support this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T09:30:21-07:00","id":532008,"title":"","content":"Excellent!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T17:58:15-07:00","id":532613,"title":"","content":"As an idea for a character...ok. But speaking as a twin....it's not something I would gel with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:55:37-07:00","id":532638,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they're not supposed to be a realistic depiction so much as a more 'mythic' version of the twins from the shining, speaking and acting in unison and the like we're aware that the idea's unrealistic, I have identical and fraternal twin cousins and the player has twin brothers (her brothers are twins). They're going to be twin fortunetellers in the circus <i>before </i>their visitation. (and as I said before, they're heavily based on Castor and Pollux)<br /> <br /> We shoot for cinematic rather than realist concepts in our scion games. Other characters include an 86yr old Japanese American Camp survivor cum Cattle Farmer master of Go, a Native American nurse-midwife working on her doctorate and a policewoman who beat the real world first patrol woman onto the streets by 3 years or so (the game is set in 1965 Kansas City).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","user":"Gnomish American","date":". 05-29-2015, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T08:49:50-07:00","id":533241,"title":"","content":"I think the mechanics aspect of it is going to be the trickiest part. Since you are allowing one player to play both characters, you have effectively doubled that player's ability to participate. It's a big advantage. Even if they are apart, they can keep the group effectively united, depending on how connected they are. If being two people means that they are getting Access to two Scions worth of powers, it's a big deal. When they are together they would be much more powerful than other characters and when they are apart they would be equal to or less than (weaker, possibly liabilities in particular circumstances, like, say, combat).<br /> <br /> The Dioskouri didn't really do this sort of thing. They were definitely 2 different people. Just like Helen and Clytemnestra were two different people (since Castor &amp; Pollux hatched out of one egg and the two ladies hatched out of the other). They were just totally cool with sharing immortality and mortality to be able to stay together. To my mind, the closest would seem to be Tiresias and his/hers was a lot more externally controlled and disadvantageous than Tina/Tanya (Tinanya?)<br /> <br /> Since we don't have access to whatever coolness might enable this in Scion Next, you are going to have to figure out how to model it. It's going to be tough to do with a Relic, since the one you have described is already an impossible Relic 6 as one doodad. Maybe it's 2 Relics that have a slight disadvantage in that only one is usable at a time? Maybe make them both Relic 4 and give each of them a cool power over the 3 Purviews and an aspect of the cool power is that they are intrinsically linked so that one exists or the other. <br /> <br /> Perhaps you could simulate the &quot;two bodies but one divine presence&quot; thing with a Ritual Maiming? Together they have the full power of one Scion and apart they have reduced stats? Maybe try to make an adjustment to Avatar that has some definite drawbacks at Hero (and Demigod) that don't crop up at God?<br /> <br /> Honestly, the way I would probably run it is to to see if everyone is okay with that player having two characters in play simultaneously and giving them each their own Relic with some 4th power that only works when the other twin &amp; amulet is present. Then having each of them take a Ritual Maiming whereby they are diminished when they are apart. It would be a big one, like 5 dots.<br /> <br /> The only time I have had this come up in my game was one player playing two different Scions who were identical twins with one receiving his Visitation from their bio-dad, Apollo and the other being gifted to Artemis. They were separated at birth and raised by completely different families. One grew up in Seattle and became a musician. The other joined the marines and became a sniper. (Guess which one was adopted by which parent? You undoubtedly guessed right). We were running two linked chronicles (one in America and one where all the characters were spec ops Scions in Iraq), so he did have the chance to play both characters at the same time. Since the sniper had a Kentucky accent, it was easy to tell which was which.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T11:59:36-07:00","id":533481,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the pendant is actually two different relics (its a 'split' pendant) I was just bouncing ideas when I said they shared powers. the only 'unique' aspect of them is that they're fate bound to BOTH siblings. The characters aren't psychic in any way that will allow for long distance communication, they're simply used as one character (including only getting one action between them) they do not, for example, get double the purview points or birthrights.<br /> <br /> I'm also making the assumption that as Castor and Pollux shared more than just their immortality. Though I DONT think I'll kill both siblings if their health track fills up. the second sibling will just be too busy mourning to act for the rest of combat and then... who knows.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}